# #6759 c11 (D-CORE-FILE-ADAPTERS1=A): cbor.reader is generic over the
# Prelude `Reader`. A program's own byte source, handing out one or two bytes
# per read, feeds it, and `loop .. in` walks the generic reader; a source that
# ends inside an array is a Truncated error at the byte it stopped, and a
# source whose reads fail surfaces as an IO EncodingError whose cause keeps the
# IOError's OS code and its errno kind. Each tier prints the same lines.
fixture: cbor_reader_pulls_from_a_programs_own_reader.fixture
step: jet check run.jet
exit: 0
step: jet run -O0 run.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = cbor_reader_pulls_from_a_programs_own_reader.out
step: jet run -O2 run.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = cbor_reader_pulls_from_a_programs_own_reader.out
step: jet build run.jet
exit: 0
step aot: built
exit: 0
stdout: = cbor_reader_pulls_from_a_programs_own_reader.out
